.TH "XmStringCreateFontList" "library call"
.nh
.SH "NAME"
\fB\%XmStringCreateFontList\fP,
\fB\%XmStringCreateFontList_r\fP \(em Create a font list from a font
.iX "XmStringCreateFontList"
.iX "font list functions" "XmStringCreateFontList"
.iX "font list functions" "XmStringCreateFontList_r"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/Xm\&.h>
.PP
\fBXmFontList \fBXmStringCreateFontList\fP\fR(
\fBXFontStruct *\fBfont\fR\fR,
\fBconst char *\fBcharset\fR\fR);
.PP
\fBXmFontList \fBXmStringCreateFontList_r\fP\fR(
\fBXFontStruct *\fBfont\fR\fR,
\fBconst char *\fBcharset\fR\fR,
\fBWidget \fBwid\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
These functions are obsolete; use \fB\%XmRenditionCreate\fP and
\fB\%XmRenderTableAddRenditions\fP\&.  They create a font list with one
entry, the font \fIfont\fP tagged \fIcharset\fP, as
\fB\%XmFontListAppendEntry\fP(NULL,
\fB\%XmFontListEntryCreate\fP(\fIcharset\fP,
\fB\%XmFONT_IS_FONT\fP, \fIfont\fP)) does\&.  The \fIwid\fP argument of
\fB\%XmStringCreateFontList_r\fP is not used\&.
.IP "\fIfont\fP" 10
Specifies the font\&.
.IP "\fIcharset\fP" 10
Specifies the tag of the entry\&.
.IP "\fIwid\fP" 10
Is not used\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
Returns a new font list, which the caller frees with
\fB\%XmFontListFree\fP\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fB\%XmFontListCreate\fP(3), \fB\%XmFontListEntryCreate\fP(3) and
\fB\%XmRenditionCreate\fP(3)\&.
